# -*- coding: ascii; tab-width: 4 -*-
Package: nasm
Version: 2.16.03
Revision: 1
Description: Netwide Assembler for x86
License: BSD
Maintainer: Daniel Johnson <daniel@daniel-johnson.org>
Homepage: https://www.nasm.us/
DescDetail: <<
	The Netwide Assembler, NASM, is an 80x86 and x86-64 assembler
	designed for portability and modularity. It supports a range of
	object file formats, including Linux and BSD a.out, ELF, Mach-O,
	16-bit and 32-bit .obj (OMF) format, COFF (including its Win32 and
	Win64 variants.) It can also output plain binary files, Intel hex
	and Motorola S-Record formats. Its syntax is designed to be simple
	and easy to understand, similar to the syntax in the Intel Software
	Developer Manual with minimal complexity. It supports all currently
	known x86 architectural extensions, and has strong support for
	macros.
<<

Source: https://www.nasm.us/pub/nasm/releasebuilds/%v/%n-%v.tar.bz2
Source-Checksum: SHA256(bef3de159bcd61adf98bb7cc87ee9046e944644ad76b7633f18ab063edb29e57)
Source2: https://www.nasm.us/pub/nasm/releasebuilds/%v/%n-%v-xdoc.tar.bz2
Source2-Checksum: SHA256(f14148fc1f7d0518966bb1ffa012b3d79b227775568b478cca65386a64e466e7)

NoSetCPPFLAGS: true
NoSetLDFLAGS: true
ConfigureParams: --docdir=%p/share/doc/%n

CompileScript: <<
	./configure %c
	make all manpages
<<

InfoTest: TestScript: make test || exit 2

# Manually install prebuilt docs since it tries to rebuild them otherwise.
InstallScript: <<
	make install DESTDIR=%d
	mkdir -p %i/share/doc/%n/html
	install -c -m 644 doc/html/* %i/share/doc/%n/html
	install -c -m 644 doc/nasmdoc.pdf doc/nasmdoc.txt %i/share/doc/%n
<<

DocFiles: AUTHORS ChangeLog CHANGES LICENSE README.md
